    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "MARY AND JOSEPH — SILENT CONNECTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "The chorus reaches a musical punctuation. The orchestration reduces rather than implying anything supernatural. Ordinary village life shifts into extreme slow motion. Mary and Joseph remain at normal speed. Villagers continue bargaining, working, carrying, reaching and crossing around them. For a moment, the audience experiences the town through Mary and Joseph."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary crosses with a handmade TOOL SATCHEL."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "I made this for you. A new tool satchel."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "For me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "Yours was falling apart."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "I was calling it well-loved."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "MARY"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "Then cherish this one instead."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "I will. Especially because you made it."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary smiles. Their hands may briefly meet naturally during the exchange, but the touch is not treated as a magical cue. Joseph puts the satchel over his shoulder. They remain together one beat longer than necessary."
    },
    {
      "type": "stage",
      "text": "Mary begins walking away. Joseph watches her one beat too long."
    },
    {
      "type": "music",
      "text": "MUSIC / MOVEMENT SNAP"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "BANG. Full tempo, sound and marketplace movement return at once. Joseph is a fraction late returning to the world; a passing villager or carried object may nearly catch him unaware."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CALEB"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "You coming?"
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "I’m coming."
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "He is still looking toward Mary."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "CALEB"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "Joseph."
    },
    {
      "type": "character",
      "text": "JOSEPH"
    },
    {
      "type": "lyric",
      "text": "I said I’m coming."
    },
